I'll be trying not to give too much spoilers... You'll probably have  
plenty of other more or less spoily answers and anyway don't hesitate to  
ask for precision on point you really want to know...

> I want to read blessed scrolls of identify until I get that big lucky
> break.  I've managed to bless and read two so far, but no luck.
> !oConfusion and Water have been really scarce and I have only two more
> identify scrolls at my disposal, both cursed.  How should I go about
> this?  Is this even an important goal right now?  It seems like a good
> idea to know what your tricks are before things get hairy.

Yes. I usually like it and my first holy water go for scrolls of identify.  
Then of enchant armor/weapon. There are several way to sort out potions  
you don't really want to use (eg hallucination or fruit juice) so that you  
can have more water at your disposal. But you're indeed at the point where  
I usually am a little short on (holy) water. Things should go better  
later...

> I also have some nice, but damaged, pieces of armor: a +4 cloak
> (orcish?), +3 elven boots, and a +2 helmet.  The cloak and boots are
> burnt; the cloak is down to +3.  The helmet is thoroughly rusty.  I
> haven't found any oil so far.  Is it possible to repair them?  I'm
> guessing that grease would protect the helmet for the future, right?
> How can I protect the burnable items?  What's the best way to deal with
> pyrolisks?  (I just want a hint for the last question.)

Yes, you can repair them. And you can protect them from fire/water/...  
Mostly by the mean (or a similar one). IIRC, grease will indeed protect  
 from rust. And from other bad things too.
Oh, yes, there is an oracle about that way to protect/repair your armor.  
It's a major fortune, iirc. Either buy enough major to have all the  
information you need or ask for it here... Yes, you'll need lot of money  
for that...

> My large cat has died.  I was otherwise occupied when it happened,
> figuring it could handle a leather golem.  Anyway, I haven't really
> missed having a pet, except when I would like buc status on an item I
> just found.  Should I bother getting a new one?  I know of a polymorph
> trap and I can obtain a leash.  Are there any interesting possibilities
> there?

Yes. It is always nice to have a pet, even not too powerful. If you have a  
polytrap at hand and enough patience, you can get almost any pet. Ever  
seen a pet Dragon, Titan or Vampire ?

For buc-iding, there is of course a far better way to do it than with pet.  
And you have it at your disposition now. But of course, it may involve to  
walk a lot...

> I keep running into Aleaxes, which seems to indicate that I've strayed
