> aligned'?  Am I in trouble?  The Aleaxes have been easy to destroy,
> anyway.

I'm afraid I don't have clues here. A charge of enlightenment is not very  
very valuable imho, so it won't be totally wasted to use it just to be  
sure.

> I ate a troll corpse.  Did that do me any good, other than keeping it
> from reanimating?

No. If it does good, then you have a message when eating it.

> It seems to me that before reading a scroll of armor enchantment, it's
> a good idea to shed your suit and put your cloak back on.  You don't
> want to use enchantments on a suit that might be destroyed if you hit a
> polymorph trap.  It seems that everything else just falls off unharmed.
>  Comments?

There is a way to definitely protect you from polytrap. It also protect  
you from lots and lots of other very bad think so it's a must have for the  
late game. Very few items do provide it unfortunately...
There is also a quite obvious way to nullify the effect of a polytrap: if  
you can choose your resulting form, then you won't break your armor.
And lots of 's'earch before moving reduce the chance of running into a  
polytrap.

Apart from that, I think you're right in only upgrading 'safe' armor. Once  
you'll be able to no more care about polytrap, then you'll want to enchant  
everything. Actually, when you want to enchant something, don't do it  
'blindly'. Remove all your armor but one, hence you'll know exactly what  
will be enchanted.

> Are there any monsters that can loot a locked chest or box?

No. But some can eat them. Read the Guidebook, there is a way to deal with  
that probelm explained it in (via engraving).

> Finally, would anyone like to give me a general plan of action for the
> near future?

Go down, kill everyone, grab the amulet and go up :-)

> My barbarian is 12th level with 138 HP and -5 AC (-6 but for the burnt

You really need to improve that AC. Try to find enough scroll/good armor  
(wear any armor you find (after buc-iding) and keep the best). An AC  
around -15 will probably be safer for the next part of the dungeon (later  
you'll want it around -25 or even down to -50 if you manage it). There is  
also a way to definitely lower your AC, using money.

