> with?), a unicorn horn, a towel, a tin opener, an oil lamp, a fire
> horn, a couple of other basic tools, some gems, and about 4000 GP.
> (This is all from memory; I might have forgotten some things.)

Try to get more money (sell everything in the dungeon to shopkeepers, or  
kill the shopkeepers if you/your pet can handle this). Buy major  
consultation from the oracle and write them down. There are some very,  
very, *very* bit of information in them (especially if you don't want to  
be spoiled).

Concerning the general plan of action :
_ maybe take some time to find better armor/improve your armor. You might  
want to do that sometime later if you don't have much trouble while going  
down.
_ Identify your stuff. You *want* to know what potions are healing because  
you'll need them. Identify your ring, there might be some very valuable  
ones in the lot.
_ Maybe consider diluting some random potions if you need more water. It's  
better if you find which you won't need but if you really need holy water,  
go for it.

_ When you decide to go down, don't be too fast but there's no need to be  
extra cautious right now. At some point you should have a message when  
entering a level. There is something to find in that level, leading to  
another dungeon branch (like the Mines or Soko) called "The Quest". I  
won't do that branch with an AC of -6. Try to go to approx -10 or -15  
before going there.
_ You can continue in the main dungeon without doing the quest. At some  
point around level 25-30 (iirc), you'll find a special level. And there  
your troubles'll begin...

_ Get pets. Especially if you know a polytrap. Get pet and polymorph them.  
Hide the polytrap under a boulder when you're not operating it with your  
pet(s) to avoid monsters walking on it. Of course, that last point require  
that you can push the boulder, hence walk safely on the polytrap...

